drawio-diagrams-skill

This product bundles the shared converter `scripts/drawio2png.mjs` (used by all eight
diagram builders), which includes third-party
software and stencil/shape assets derived from:

1. draw.io — https://github.com/jgraph/drawio/tree/v29.6.6 (tag v29.6.6)
   and draw.io Desktop — https://github.com/jgraph/drawio-desktop
   Copyright (c) 2006-2025, JGraph Holdings Ltd (draw.io Ltd)
   Copyright (c) 2006-2025, draw.io AG
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
   (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

   `scripts/drawio2png.mjs` bundles the mxGraph / draw.io shape, stencil and
   default-style assets taken from that tag (the minified `shapes.min.js`,
   the stencil XML sets under `src/main/webapp/stencils`, the default and dark
   style sheets, and the built-in shape code), recompressed for embedding.
   The additional terms for icon sets and stencil libraries quoted below apply
   to those assets.

2. @resvg/resvg-wasm — https://github.com/thx/resvg-js/tree/v2.6.2
   (npm package `@resvg/resvg-wasm`, version 2.6.2)
   Copyright (c) 2019 - 2023, the resvg-js authors
   Licensed under the Mozilla Public License, Version 2.0
   (the full license text is available at
   https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/MPL/2.0/).

   The embedded WebAssembly binary (`index_bg.wasm` of the npm package) is an
   unmodified, base64-encoded copy of the build artifact published in npm
   `@resvg/resvg-wasm@2.6.2`, stored inside `scripts/drawio2png.mjs` so the
   converter runs offline with zero installation.

   The wasm-bindgen JavaScript glue code from that package (originally
   published as `index.mjs` / `index.js`, together with `wasm-binding.ts`) is
   NOT kept as a separate file: it was integrated directly into
   `scripts/drawio2png.mjs` as executable JavaScript, so it is a MODIFIED
   version of the original MPL-2.0 Source Code Form. The modifications: the
   package's public asynchronous entry point (which loads `index_bg.wasm` from
   a file path or network URL) is not used -- the converter instead decodes the
   base64 blob above and instantiates it synchronously with
   `new WebAssembly.Module/Instance`, feeding the result into the glue's
   `__wbg_finalize_init`; the module wrapper was unwrapped and the glue was
   renamed to internal converter symbols. The original unused fetch/file-
   loading glue lines are otherwise retained verbatim.

   SCOPE OF THE MPL-2.0 COVERED SOFTWARE. Inside `scripts/drawio2png.mjs` the
   MPL-2.0 part is delimited by the two comment markers

       // BEGIN MPL-2.0 COVERED SOFTWARE (@resvg/resvg-wasm v2.6.2)
       // END MPL-2.0 COVERED SOFTWARE (@resvg/resvg-wasm v2.6.2)

   Everything between those markers (the base64-encoded, unmodified
   `index_bg.wasm` and the wasm-bindgen JavaScript glue adapted for
   synchronous initialization) is MPL-2.0 covered software. These
   modifications remain under MPL-2.0 and this project does not relicense them.

   WHERE THE SOURCE CODE FORM OF THE MODIFIED VERSION IS AVAILABLE. The
   modified Source Code Form is distributed with this product: the block
   between the BEGIN / END markers inside `scripts/drawio2png.mjs` -- this very
   file, as shipped in this repository / distribution archive -- is itself the
   Source Code Form of the modified glue. It is readable, unobfuscated,
   uncompressed JavaScript, so no additional download is needed to obtain the
   modified version. The unmodified upstream Source Code Form of the same
   version remains available at
   https://github.com/thx/resvg-js/tree/v2.6.2 (npm `@resvg/resvg-wasm@2.6.2`),
   and the full MPL-2.0 text at https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/MPL/2.0/.

   `scripts/drawio2png.mjs` as a whole is therefore a Larger Work / Combined
